  "body": {
    "id": "lem:penalized-cancellation",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(c\\in\\mathcal C\\), the first-order condition gives \\(a_c=cg_c\\), and hence \\(\\psi^W_c-c\\psi^K_c=\\phi^W_c-c\\phi^K_c\\) almost surely.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(c\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal C\\)",
      "\\(a_c\\)",
      "\\(g_c\\)",
      "\\(\\psi^W_c\\)",
      "\\(\\psi^K_c\\)",
      "\\(\\phi^W_c\\)",
      "\\(\\phi^K_c\\)",
      "\\(\\lambda_{\\mathrm{FRX}}\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:unique-optimizer",
      "ass:uniform-interior",
      "ass:smooth-criterion",
      "def:oracle-path",
      "def:frx-penalty-map",
      "def:joint-influence"
    ],
    "justification": "The identity separates oracle-path uncertainty from implemented-rule evaluation and is a sharp implementation check.",
    "gap": "FangRidderXie2026 Theorem 5 derives fixed-\\(\\lambda_{\\mathrm{FRX}}\\) efficient doubly robust optimizer inference but does not state this joint welfare--divergence cancellation along a penalty path.",
    "consumer": "Software can test the identity at every plotted preference before trusting covariance or regret calculations.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(c\\in\\mathcal C\\).  Assumption \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}uniform\\mbox{-}interior}\\) places \\(\\theta_c\\) in the interior of \\(\\Theta\\), and Assumption \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}smooth\\mbox{-}criterion}\\) makes \\(M_c\\) differentiable there.  Fermat's first-order condition, applied to the unique optimizer in Assumption \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}unique\\mbox{-}optimizer}\\), is therefore\n\\[\n 0=\\nabla_\\theta M_c(\\theta_c)\n   =\\nabla_\\theta W(\\theta_c)-c\\nabla_\\theta K(\\theta_c)\n   =a_c-cg_c.\n\\]\nThus \\(a_c=cg_c\\).  Substitution into Definition\n\\(\\mathrm{def{:}joint\\mbox{-}influence}\\) gives, pointwise in \\(O\\),\n\\[\n \\psi_c^W-c\\psi_c^K\n =\\phi_c^W-c\\phi_c^K+(a_c-cg_c)^\\top\\psi_c^\\theta\n =\\phi_c^W-c\\phi_c^K.\n\\]\nThe correspondence \\(\\lambda_{\\mathrm{FRX}}=c\\) in Definition\n\\(\\mathrm{def{:}frx\\mbox{-}penalty\\mbox{-}map}\\) confirms that the same coefficient multiplies the divergence term; no rescaling enters this cancellation.",
